STYLE: The permanent house of a grand hand-made toy theatre, built from painted corrugated cardboard and gilded carving. Opaque matte gouache with visible brush strokes and real gold leaf. Raw cardboard brown at the cut edges. Grand, warm and a little worn, like a beloved old theatre.
REFERENCES: Image 1 is the look reference for paint, gold leaf and cardboard. Do not copy its sun and moon ornaments or its scenery.
SUBJECT: The front of the theatre: a proscenium arch seen straight on. Two gilded columns with laurel garlands. A deep crimson velvet valance with gold fringe and gold tassels across the top of the opening. Above it, a gilded crest of laurel leaves, two lyres and small stars around a blank oval cartouche with nothing inside. The base of the arch is a dark wood apron with gold trim. Neutral ornament only: no sun, no moon, no faces, no figures.
COMPOSITION: The arch fills the whole frame. The stage opening inside the arch is a large clean rectangle with a slightly arched top, and it is completely transparent: no curtain, no stage, no scenery, no background in the opening. Transparent background. No text, no letters, no logos, no watermark.
